  "details": "When someone has an animation that manipulates the location of the head (or the entire avatar including the head)\nThe scale of the nameplates can flicker momentarily.\nMy guess is that nameplates scale by distance but are a tick behind on the scale they get set at. So if someone has a headbone that animates 100 meters away and then comes back instantly it will show the 100m away sized nameplate for a single frame before adjusting back into its normal size.\nI've heard people that are photosensitive complain about this. So might be good to look into this.",
